### Feature-First Organization
- Organize code by features instead of technical layers
- Each feature is a self-contained module with its own implementation of all layers
- Core or shared functionality goes in a separate 'core' directory
- Features should have minimal dependencies on other features
- Common directory structure for each feature:


lib/
├── core/                          
│   ├── error/                     # Global error handling, custom exceptions
│   ├── network/                   # Network config, interceptors, API client
│   ├── utils/                     # Utility functions, extensions, formatters
│   └── widgets/                   # Reusable global widgets (e.g. custom buttons)
├── features/                      
│   ├── feature_a/                 
│   │   ├── data/                  
│   │   │   ├── datasources/       
│   │   │   │   ├── local/         # Handles local storage: DB, cache, shared prefs
│   │   │   │   │   └── user_local_data_source.dart
│   │   │   │   └── remote/        # Handles API requests and remote data fetching
│   │   │   │       └── user_remote_data_source.dart
│   │   │   ├── models/            # DTOs (Data Transfer Objects) + JSON serialization
│   │   │   └── repositories/      # Repository implementations (combine local & remote)
│   │   ├── domain/                
│   │   │   ├── entities/          # Business logic objects (pure, no Flutter code)
│   │   │   ├── repositories/      # Abstract repository interfaces for DI
│   │   │   └── usecases/          # Business rules, single-responsibility actions
│   │   └── presentation/          
│   │       ├── bloc/              # State management (Bloc/Cubit)
│   │       ├── pages/             # Screens and navigation entry points
│   │       └── widgets/           # Feature-specific widgets (UI components)
│   └── feature_b/                 # Same structure for other features
└── main.dart                      # Application entry point
